cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use docpluck in research, please cite the version you used (docpluck --version prints it)."
title: "docpluck: Text and statistic extraction from academic papers"
abstract: >-
  A Python library and command-line tool that extracts text, sections, tables and
  figures from academic papers in PDF, DOCX and HTML, canonicalises statistical
  notation for automated checks of the published record, records every fallback it
  took per document, and reports the exact engine versions behind each output.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Feldman
    given-names: Gilad
    affiliation: "University of Innsbruck"
repository-code: "https://github.com/giladfeldman/docpluck"
url: "https://docpluck.app"
license: MIT
version: "2.4.148"
date-released: "2026-09-28"
keywords:
  - meta-science
  - PDF extraction
  - text mining
  - statistical reporting
  - research integrity
  - reproducibility
